1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:02,680
Move one date, Tuesday to Friday,

2
00:00:02,680 --> 00:00:04,760
and six bookings break at once.

3
00:00:04,760 --> 00:00:08,280
By hand, that's about 18 steps on six websites.

4
00:00:08,280 --> 00:00:11,670
Cancel one too early and you're left with nothing.

5
00:00:11,710 --> 00:00:13,710
CONTINUITY makes it two decisions.

6
00:00:13,710 --> 00:00:17,320
Say what changed, then approve the exact plan.

7
00:00:17,360 --> 00:00:21,000
It's an open agentic website that coordinates other companies'

8
00:00:21,040 --> 00:00:24,960
agentic websites. Each provider runs its own site and

9
00:00:24,960 --> 00:00:27,600
agent network on a different origin.

10
00:00:27,600 --> 00:00:29,360
No backend in the middle,

11
00:00:29,360 --> 00:00:31,370
no shared database.

12
00:00:31,410 --> 00:00:32,890
This is the live site.

13
00:00:32,930 --> 00:00:35,250
I describe the change in plain English,

14
00:00:35,250 --> 00:00:37,650
and it becomes rules it can't break.

15
00:00:37,650 --> 00:00:40,130
Then I switch on a real-world failure.

16
00:00:40,130 --> 00:00:42,720
The moving crew is full on Friday.

17
00:00:42,760 --> 00:00:45,320
Only three of six bookings are affected.

18
00:00:45,320 --> 00:00:48,840
Four providers are asked, two are never contacted.

19
00:00:48,840 --> 00:00:51,800
The crew is recovered through an overflow partner and

20
00:00:51,800 --> 00:00:55,620
replacements are held, while my originals stay active.

21
00:00:55,660 --> 00:00:57,820
Three plans compared on changes,

22
00:00:57,820 --> 00:00:59,180
cost, and speed.

23
00:00:59,180 --> 00:01:03,700
The winner moves the fewest bookings for €659

24
00:01:03,740 --> 00:01:05,450
under my cap.

25
00:01:05,490 --> 00:01:07,330
Nothing happens without me.

26
00:01:07,330 --> 00:01:10,370
My approval is bound to the exact operations,

27
00:01:10,370 --> 00:01:12,130
prices, and providers.

28
00:01:12,130 --> 00:01:15,570
Change one fee, and it no longer matches.

29
00:01:15,610 --> 00:01:18,730
I approve. These are the providers' own pages,

30
00:01:18,730 --> 00:01:20,410
loaded cross-origin.

31
00:01:20,410 --> 00:01:22,570
Each one receives a signed receipt,

32
00:01:22,570 --> 00:01:25,930
checks it itself, and only then moves my booking.

33
00:01:25,930 --> 00:01:29,950
PowerFlow was consulted and correctly left alone.

34
00:01:30,410 --> 00:01:32,010
Every step is auditable.

35
00:01:32,010 --> 00:01:35,850
A hash-chained log, exactly what each provider saw,

36
00:01:35,850 --> 00:01:38,730
and 42 failure scenarios you can replay in the

37
00:01:38,730 --> 00:01:43,460
browser. Zero cancel calls in 180 runs.

38
00:01:43,500 --> 00:01:45,340
And it's not just moving house.

39
00:01:45,340 --> 00:01:48,380
The same engine re-plans a surgery or a delayed

40
00:01:48,380 --> 00:01:49,960
freight shipment.

41
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:54,340
CONTINUITY, one change, every commitment re-aligned.
